# Release [[.Name]]

The generated GitHub Actions workflow tests all six native OS/architecture targets
and uses GoReleaser for archives and checksums. A pushed `v*` tag publishes to the
current repository's GitHub Releases. Initialising the project does not authorise
pushing a release tag or creating external infrastructure.

Before choosing a destination, inspect the repository remote and existing CI,
search accessible organisation repositories for taps, Scoop buckets and shared
publishing workflows, and inspect local registry configuration for Artifactory or
other established destinations. Report credential availability without displaying
or copying values. Do not ask a nontechnical user to identify infrastructure that
you can discover. If access is unavailable, state what could not be checked.

Verify the CLI's location relative to the repository root. GitHub only discovers
workflows in the root `.github/workflows/`. For a monorepo, integrate the generated
jobs there with the CLI's working directory and path to its Go module/configuration.
Do not replace existing workflows. The scaffold assumes a dedicated CLI repo root.

Prefer existing infrastructure that supports the artefacts and intended audience.
Internal Artifactory may be appropriate for colleagues but insufficient for public
users. Resolve a consequential ambiguity in plain language. Existing credentials
establish feasibility, not permission to publish. Preserve existing access controls.

When no suitable destination exists, offer to create a reusable, multi-project
publishing repository from a template. Once accepted, create and configure it using
available provider tools. Homebrew and Scoop use owned repositories, while WinGet
requires catalogue submissions. Do not claim Loop has an automated provisioner:
this version provides the workflow and guidance, not provider-specific setup code.

Configure the selected destination in the release workflow/GoReleaser configuration
using the existing CI credential mechanism. The default GitHub release recipe is a
working starting point, not evidence that GitHub is the company's preferred channel.
Do not commit tokens, introduce a credential vault or bypass OS security checks.
Signing/notarisation requires publisher-owned credentials and may involve costs.

Before an authorised release, commit `go.sum`, run the project tests and validate
`.goreleaser.yaml` with the pinned GoReleaser version from the workflow. Exercise a
snapshot release. Confirm that the six native CI jobs pass at the intended commit.
Push the agreed semantic version tag only within the user's release authorisation.
Verify artefacts and publication results, and distinguish a submitted catalogue
update from an accepted one. Do not overwrite edited scaffold files during upgrades.
